.TH NIXOS 1 "" "NixOS Flake Helper" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
nixos \- unified wrapper for managing the NixOS flake

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nixos
.RI [ command ] " [args]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B nixos
command is a user-facing wrapper for managing the NixOS flake
.B github:sotormd/nixos.
It provides a curated set of high-level commands for carrying out
routine tasks.

When invoked without a command,
.B nixos
displays the flake directory tree with files listed first.

If an unrecognized command is provided, it is dispatched verbatim
inside the flake directory
.RB ( $NIXOS_DIR ),
allowing arbitrary commands to be run relative to the flake.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B test
.br
Test the current configuration.
.br
Does not create a boot entry.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B boot
.br
Make current configuration the boot default.
.br
Does not activate the current configuration.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B switch
.br
Switch to the current configuration.
.br
Creates a boot entry.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B commit
.br
Switch to and commit the current configuration.
.br
Creates a boot entry and a Git commit.
.br
Roles: laptop only

.TP
.B update " [inputs...]"
.br
Update flake inputs in flake.lock.
.br
If no inputs are specified, all inputs are updated.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B digest
.br
Get checksum of variables and secrets.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B format
.br
Format the flake using nixfmt.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B perms
.br
Fix file ownership and permissions in the flake.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B purge
.br
Garbage collect old generations.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B repair
.br
Attempt to repair the nix store.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B edit " <vars|sops>"
.br
Edit variables file or sops-nix secrets.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B serverpush " <path>"
.br
Push the local flake to server:<path> .
.br
Roles: laptop only

.TP
.B help
.br
Display a brief usage summary and exit.
.br
Roles: laptop, server

.TP
.B init <command> [args]
.br
Bootstrap this flake.
See documentation for more information

.SH DISPATCH BEHAVIOR
If a command does not match one of the built-in subcommands,
.B nixos
executes it directly inside
.BR $NIXOS_DIR .

This allows convenient interaction with the flake repository, such as:

.nf
nixos git status
nixos cat flake.nix | wl-copy
nixos vi modules/common/firewall.nix
.fi

.SH LOCKING
To prevent concurrent execution,
.B nixos
creates a lockfile at
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nixos-script.lock
for the following commands:
test, boot, switch, commit, update, purge, format, perms, and init.

.SH NOTES
All commands are intended to be run through the
.B nixos
wrapper and not executed directly.
The wrapper automatically escalates privileges using
.B sudo
when required.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B $NIXOS_DIR/docs/scripts.md
Full documentation.

